# Origin: legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/maths-errors.chk
# Milestone: M6 Wave 2 (Phase 11 partial port)
#
# Legacy fixture asserts:
#   - `1 / 0` raises `/: division by 0` — v1.0 returns IEEE-754 `inf`
#     (REVIVAL §14.x divergence: arithmetic is float-IEEE-754, no
#     domain-error wrapping at the bytecode level).
#   - `Math.sqrt(-10.0) / log(-10.0) / acos(-100.0) / asin(-100.0)`
#     raise domain-specific diagnostics — v0.6.1 has no Math.sqrt /
#     log / acos / asin (Math has only constants pi/e/nan/infinity).
#   - `Math.sqr("foo")` raises `sqr: lookup failed: sqr` — v1.0 also
#     raises a sqr lookup failure but via the Float atom-proto fallback.
#
# This port keeps the legacy file's "lookup failure on missing Math
# slot" assertion (the only one that remains semantically sharp at
# v1.0) and documents the IEEE-754 inf divergence.
#
# Wave-2 deferred (full port): all Math.{sqrt,log,acos,asin,sqr}
# methods + their domain-error diagnostics; `1 % 0` parsing (legacy
# ran modulo-by-0 as an integer-only operation).  See PORT_NOTES.md.

# `1 / 0` returns inf at v1.0 (IEEE-754).  Legacy raised
# `/: division by 0`.  Documented divergence; not a bug.
1 / 0
[00000000] inf

# Math at v0.6.1 ships constants only; method lookups fail as
# `slot 'NAME' not found` via the SELF proto-walk diagnostic (the
# method-call dispatch opcode introduced at v1.6 S42; pre-v1.6 the
# message read "GETSLOT:" since method dispatch went through plain
# OP_GETSLOT + the deleted vm->last_recv side channel).
Math.sqrt(4)
[00000001:error] !!! TypeError: SELF: slot 'sqrt' not found

Math.log(1)
[00000002:error] !!! TypeError: SELF: slot 'log' not found

Math.sqr(2)
[00000003:error] !!! TypeError: SELF: slot 'sqr' not found

# Math.nan exists; Math.nan.isNaN() routes through the Float atom-
# proto installed at Phase 5.
Math.nan.isNaN()
[00000004] true
